# From Chaos to Systems: The Engineering Foundations of Organization Theory, 1879-1932.

**Authors:** Shenhav, Yehouda

## Abstract
Traces the genesis of the systems paradigm in organizational study in the United States to 19th-century engineering practices, based on primary data from three professional journals. The systems paradigm evolved from three forces: the professionalization of mechanical engineering, the political culture of Progressivism, and the politics of labor unrest. (MLH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ519753

